  "estimatedMinutes": 3,
  "statement": "Let \\(Q(z)\\) and \\(R(z)\\) be the unique polynomials such that \\[ \\begin{aligned} &z^{2021}+1 \\\\ &\\quad = (z^2+z+1)Q(z)+R(z) \\end{aligned} \\] and the degree of \\(R\\) is less than \\(2.\\) What is \\(R(z)?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(-z\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2021\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(z+1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2z+1\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2021-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(z^3\\equiv 1\\pmod{z^2+z+1}\\) and \\(2021=3\\cdot 673+2,\\) we have \\(z^{2021}\\equiv z^2.\\)\n\nSo \\(z^{2021}+1\\equiv z^2+1.\\) Reducing further with \\(z^2\\equiv -z-1,\\) this is \\(-z-1+1=-z.\\)\n\nTherefore \\(R(z)=-z.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Modulo \\(z^2+z+1\\) we have \\(z^3\\equiv 1,\\) since \\(z^3-1=(z-1)(z^2+z+1)\\)",
        "Reduce the exponent \\(2021\\) modulo \\(3,\\) then reduce \\(z^2\\) using \\(z^2\\equiv -z-1\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
